particle correlation measurement, the relative \(\eta\) difference between the particles is considered. This has particular implications for the definitions of the measurement interval and how the centrality determination is made.

A strong bias exists if the measurement of \(N_{ch}\) overlaps with the measurement interval in \(\eta\) space. Therefore, there are three \(\eta\) regions used to determine reference multiplicity:

